2. Core Mission Directive

Build a full-stack web application where farmers, agronomists, and agri-extension officers upload photos of crops (leaves, fruits, stems, whole-field shots) and receive AI-powered visual diagnosis and actionable advisory.

The system must replace slow, inconsistent manual field inspection by:

Seeing: using a vision-capable AI model (Google Gemini via @google/genai) to identify the crop, detect visible disease, pest damage, nutrient deficiency, water or heat stress, and weed pressure.
Localizing: returning normalized bounding regions for every detected problem area so the UI can draw them on the image.
Judging: scoring severity, confidence, and urgency in a consistent, structured way.
Advising: producing a prioritized treatment plan (cultural, organic, chemical-as-last-resort), prevention steps, and a monitoring schedule.
Remembering: storing every scan so the same field can be re-scanned over time and the AI can detect progression, spread, or recovery (visual anomaly tracking).
Presenting: delivering everything inside a 3D, interactive, earthy, theme-aligned interface (no neon).

The mission is complete only when a farmer can sign up, upload a photo, see detected problem areas drawn over their image, read a clear treatment plan, and track the field's health over weeks, all in one smooth, deployed experience.

3. Product Goal

Problem Statement (use verbatim in README): Smallholder farmers and field officers rely on manual visual inspection of crops. This is slow, depends on scarce expert availability, produces inconsistent diagnoses between inspectors, and misses early-stage anomalies, which causes avoidable yield loss and over- or mis-use of pesticides.

Solution Description (use verbatim in README): AgriLens is an AI-powered Computer Vision advisory platform. Users upload crop images; a vision-capable Gemini model analyzes them server-side, identifies the crop, detects diseases, pests, nutrient deficiencies and stress patterns, localizes affected regions on the image, scores severity, and returns a structured, prioritized advisory. Repeated scans of the same field are compared to detect progression and anomalies. A 3D interactive interface makes the results intuitive and engaging.

Primary goals:

Reduce diagnosis time from days (waiting for an expert) to under 30 seconds.
Make diagnoses consistent and structured (same schema, every time).
Catch early anomalies through scan-over-scan comparison.
Promote responsible input use (cultural and organic first, chemical as last resort, with safety notes).
Be demonstrable in a 3–5 minute demo video.
