22. Acceptance Criteria

The project is DONE only when ALL of the following are true:

Functional

 A new user can register, log in, and log out; protected routes redirect when unauthenticated.
 A user can create, edit, and delete fields; no user can see or modify another user's data (verified by manual test with two accounts, returning 404).
 Uploading 1–4 valid images produces a completed scan with a validated diagnosis and treatment plan within ~40 s.
 Invalid files (wrong type, oversized, >4 files, disguised non-images) are rejected with clear messages.
 Bounding boxes render correctly over images and sync with finding cards.
 A non-plant or blurry image yields unclear / usable=false with retake tips instead of a confident wrong diagnosis.
 Comparing two scans of the same field returns a validated progression report with a status and anomaly alerts.
 Chat answers are grounded in the scan and stay on topic; injection attempts in notes or chat do not change behavior.
 Dashboard shows accurate counts, severity distribution, trends, and a cached weekly insight (and a proper empty state with no data).
 Report export works.

AI & Security

 GEMINI_API_KEY appears nowhere in client bundles, network responses, logs, or the repository (verify with a bundle grep).
 Every AI response is JSON-schema-requested and Zod-validated; malformed output triggers one repair retry, then a 502.
 RLS policies exist and are enabled on all user-data tables; queries run through withUser.
 Rate limits and AI quotas function and return 429.
 npm audit shows no critical vulnerabilities.

UI / UX

 The interface is 3D and interactive (hero scene, leaf inspector, tilt cards, parallax) and follows the earthy palette with no neon, no glow effects, no saturated cyan/magenta/lime anywhere.
 Works on mobile (360 px) through desktop; camera capture works on mobile browsers.
 3D degrades gracefully (no WebGL or reduced motion → static fallback), with no console errors.
 Every page has loading, empty, and error states; keyboard navigation and visible focus rings work; text contrast meets WCAG AA.

Delivery

 Public GitHub repository contains the full client and server code, .env.example files, schema.sql, README, and DEMO_SCRIPT.md.
 Frontend deployed (Vercel) and backend deployed (Render) with the database connected; the deployed app works end to end.
 No placeholder text, lorem ipsum, TODO comments, or fake data remain.
